Chapter: LinearShadow
  cites Codex chapter General

 A binder that shadows a linear parameter's name introduces a fresh,
 non-linear value. Uses of the shadow must not be counted against the
 linear parameter. Here `n` (linear) is consumed exactly once in
 `n + 1`; the inner `let n = 7` shadows it and is used freely.

Section: Definitions

  consume : linear Integer -> Integer
  consume (n) = let base = n + 1
   in let n = 7
   in base + n + n

  opening : Integer
  opening = consume 41

